      "fund": "Substack / Inside Arbitrage",
      "date": "June 2025",
      "summary": "The research memo analyzes Deckers' expanded $2.25 billion share buyback program (~12% of market cap) backed by over $2 billion in cash and zero debt. Despite 5-year CAGRs of 19% in revenue and 32% in EPS driven by stellar momentum in HOKA (+46.7%) and UGG (+11.3%), the stock dropped sharply on Vietnam tariff concerns ($150 million gross headwind). The author argues that short-term fears are significantly overblown and that aggressive management share buybacks at 12-13x P/E signal an exceptional risk/reward setup.",
