      "title": "Deckers Brands / DECK is undervalued. LONG",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "August 2026",
      "summary": "This detailed pitch presents a 5-year DCF model using FY2026 financial filings, arguing Deckers is severely mispriced at ~$97 per share versus an intrinsic fair value of $225 per share. With $1.603 billion in net cash, zero debt, and $1.05 billion in FCF (11.3x EV/FCF), DECK trades at a depressed 13.8x P/E multiple relative to its historical 22x+ average. Continued double-digit top-line momentum across HOKA and international growth channels offers over 130% upside as valuation multiples re-rate toward historical mid-cycle norms.",
