    {
      "title": "Deckers (DECK): 52% Drop, 104% Upside? A DCF Case Study",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "September 2025",
      "summary": "The write-up conducts a ten-year tapered DCF valuation following Deckers' 52% drawdown from $224 to $105 per share, establishing an intrinsic equity value of $32.9 billion ($215.80 per share). Utilizing Damodaran-based WACC methodology (7.2%) and historical 22.3% EBITDA margins, the model demonstrates that Wall Street's fear of tariff headwinds and conservative management guidance significantly underappreciate brand durability in UGG and HOKA. Sensitivity analysis reveals a substantial margin of safety with over 104% implied upside.",
